= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Ten questions designed in authentic CUET UG single-correct style. The official marking scheme awards $+5$ for each correct answer and deducts $-1$ for every incorrect answer.

#mcq(1, [Which year marked the formal end of the single-party 'Congress System' at the Centre, inaugurating a quarter-century of coalition governments?], (
  [1977], [1984], [1989], [1996],
))

#mcq(2, [The National Front government led by Prime Minister V.P. Singh in 1989 was supported from the outside by which unique ideological pairing?], (
  [Congress and CPI], [BJP and the Left Front], [AIADMK and DMK], [Janata Party and Swatantra Party],
))

#mcq(3, [Who chaired the Second Backward Classes Commission appointed by the Morarji Desai Janata Party government in 1978?], (
  [Kaka Kalelkar], [B.P. Mandal], [Jagjivan Ram], [Charan Singh],
))

#mcq(4, [In which historic verdict did the Supreme Court validate the 27% OBC reservation while imposing a 50% quota ceiling and excluding the creamy layer?], (
  [Kesavananda Bharati Case (1973)], [Minerva Mills Case (1980)], [Indra Sawhney Case (1992)], [S.R. Bommai Case (1994)],
))

#mcq(5, [Which Prime Minister formulated the foreign policy doctrine that India must extend non-reciprocal unilateral goodwill to smaller South Asian neighbours?], (
  [P.V. Narasimha Rao], [H.D. Deve Gowda], [I.K. Gujral], [Atal Bihari Vajpayee],
))

#mcq(6, [Which was the first non-Congress coalition government in post-independence India to complete a full five-year term in office?], (
  [Janata Party Government (1977–1982)], [United Front Government (1996–2001)], [National Democratic Alliance (1999–2004)], [United Progressive Alliance (2004–2009)],
))

#mcq(7, [According to Yogendra Yadav's framework, the 'Second Democratic Upsurge' in Indian politics was primarily marked by:], (
  [The introduction of universal adult suffrage in the 1950s], [The electoral mobilization and assertion of Other Backward Classes (OBCs)], [The adoption of Liberalisation, Privatisation, and Globalisation in 1991], [The youth-driven aspirational voting post-2014],
))

#mcq(8, [Which landmark rights-based act guaranteeing 100 days of rural wage employment was enacted by the UPA-I government in 2005?], (
  [Right to Information Act], [MGNREGA], [Right to Education Act], [National Food Security Act],
))

#mcq(9, [The minority government led by Prime Minister Chandra Shekhar in 1990–1991 came to power with the outside support of which party?], (
  [Bharatiya Janata Party], [Left Front], [Indian National Congress], [Telugu Desam Party],
))

#mcq(10, [In the 2014 general election, how many seats did the Bharatiya Janata Party win on its own to achieve the first single-party majority in 30 years?], (
  [272], [282], [303], [336],
